      "program_name": "Permanent Local Housing Allocation (PLHA), County formula allocation and PLHA development loans",
      "administering_agency": "Fresno County Department of Public Works and Planning, Community Development Division",
      "funding_type": "loan",
      "typical_award_size": "HCD formula allocations: $1,643,348 (2019), $2,554,272 (2020), $2,810,897 (2021), estimated five-year 2019-2023 total $9,860,088; 2024-2028 plan estimated $7,209,494 with $1,153,519 (2024) and $1,235,588 (2025). Cycle One Year Three funds of $2,670,353 were committed by resolution on February 10, 2026 to Cherry Crossing II in Sanger (64 units, Self-Help Enterprises) after the Sanger Modular project missed a November 1, 2025 commitment deadline; Sendero Commons carries a replacement PLHA reservation of $2,364,219. The County retains 5% ($140,544 of Year Three) for administration.",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not published; whole-year allocations of about $2.4 million to $2.7 million go to one project.",
      "affordability_requirement": "55-year affordability; the County's PLHA plan targets households to 80% AMI with half the PLHA-assisted units at or below 60% AMI and half at or below 80% AMI (new construction or rehabilitation of multifamily rental).",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "acquisition-rehab"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "annual NOFA",
      "next_deadline": "PLHA is offered through the combined Affordable Housing Development NOFO (January to March each year). HCD commitment deadlines drive timing: Year Three had to be committed by April 30, 2026 or revert to the state Multifamily Housing Program.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Fresno County splits housing work three ways: the Department of Public Works and Planning, Community Development Division (ComDev) runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA and the annual Affordable Housing Development NOFO; the County Administrative Office's new Office of Housing and Homelessness (OHH, created November 18, 2025) administers HHAP, the Continuum of Care and Transitional Rent and is absorbing housing programs from Behavioral Health and ComDev (Phase 2 approved November 3, 2026); and the Department of Behavioral Health co-applies for Homekey+ and NPLH and funds BHSA housing. Fresno Housing (the joint City and County Housing Authorities) is the dominant developer and voucher source. The City of Fresno and Clovis are separate entitlements with their own programs (Pass 3). fresnocountyca.gov and fresnohousing.org open normally; Board records are on fresnocounty.legistar.com and the Legistar web API client 'fresnocounty'. PLHA is the County's largest non-federal source and is conditional on HCD review (allow at least 45 days after County approval). The County has concentrated each year's allocation on a single tax credit project in a JPA city (Sanger twice); it is paired with a HOME or HOME-CHDO loan at 0% or 3% simple and 55-year covenants. Source is the February 10, 2026 Board resolution (file 25-1504); allocation figures from the County's PLHA standard agreement (fresno-county-plha-agreement.pdf) and HCD's 2024-2028 PLHA NOFA tables.",
      "source_url": "https://fresnocounty.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=77181&GUID=D6D23411-4846-4C95-8274-C95360065D4F",
      "record_id": "d427ef2bcc",
      "cycle_notes": "",
      "eligible_project_detail": [
        "multifamily rental new construction",
        "multifamily rehabilitation"
      ],
      "next_deadline_date": "2026-04-30",
      "deadline_check": "past_date",
