      "funding_type": "grant",
      "typical_award_size": "Sendero Commons, Sanger (88 units, 87 PSH at 30% AMI, 45 veteran units; total development cost $54,007,788): Homekey+ $29,853,131 ($26,295,016 capital, $3,558,115 operating; award notice March 20, 2026, standard agreement approved October 20, 2026), NPLH Round 4 $18,147,660 ($10,000,038 capital, $8,147,660 operating, transferred from the failed Libre Commons project), HHIP $530,000, local contributions $5,476,959 (County HOME-ARP $2,500,000 and PLHA $2,364,219). County committed 20 years of supportive services ($10,241,756) and a 20-year rental subsidy on 42 units through Transitional Rent and BHSA ($15,314,934). The County also co-applied with Fresno Housing for Davu Village (former Parkside Inn, 1415 W. Olive Avenue, Fresno; total cost $22,362,000; resolution up to $35,000,000, April 3, 2025 application).",
      "per_unit_cap": "Homekey+ and NPLH per-unit limits set by HCD.",
      "affordability_requirement": "Homekey+ and NPLH: all assisted units for households with serious mental illness or behavioral health needs experiencing or at risk of homelessness, 30% AMI, Coordinated Entry referrals, 55-year regulatory agreement.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "supportive housing",
        "interim housing"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "Homekey+ applications are accepted by HCD over the counter while funds last; the County selected its co-applicants through Behavioral Health MOUs approved February 11, 2025 (RH Community Builders and Fresno Housing). A developer seeking County sponsorship should approach Behavioral Health and the Office of Housing and Homelessness with a site and a services plan.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Fresno County splits housing work three ways: the Department of Public Works and Planning, Community Development Division (ComDev) runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA and the annual Affordable Housing Development NOFO; the County Administrative Office's new Office of Housing and Homelessness (OHH, created November 18, 2025) administers HHAP, the Continuum of Care and Transitional Rent and is absorbing housing programs from Behavioral Health and ComDev (Phase 2 approved November 3, 2026); and the Department of Behavioral Health co-applies for Homekey+ and NPLH and funds BHSA housing. Fresno Housing (the joint City and County Housing Authorities) is the dominant developer and voucher source. The City of Fresno and Clovis are separate entitlements with their own programs (Pass 3). fresnocountyca.gov and fresnohousing.org open normally; Board records are on fresnocounty.legistar.com and the Legistar web API client 'fresnocounty'. The County's role is co-applicant, services provider and rental subsidy source rather than capital lender; the capital stack at Sendero Commons is state money (Homekey+ and NPLH, about 67% of cost) plus County HOME-ARP and PLHA. NPLH Round 4 money was reallocated once already, so timing of state agreements has run three to five years behind initial awards. Source is the October 20, 2026 Board item (file 26-0992).",
      "source_url": "https://fresnocounty.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=78181&GUID=2D0CCF41-0D9A-4DF6-A269-F6AB899B5FF1",
